What I learned
The biggest challenge was handling the massive size of the NOAA CSV file on Windows. 
Direct conversion to GeoParquet using ogr2ogr often crashed the terminal or produced files with missing geometry due to memory limits. 
I learned that converting to GeoJSON first is a much more stable intermediate step. 
GeoJSON is a standard, analysis-ready format that preserves geometry perfectly and works reliably in QGIS, making it a superior choice for this specific dataset and OS environment.

